# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# DENY BY DEFAULT.
#
# Nothing in this repo is tracked unless it is explicitly allowed
# below. A new file is untracked until someone opts it in, so
# forgetting to update this file can never leak a creator's data.
#
# Adding a new source dir later? Add "!src/**" style lines below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Ignore everything...
*

# 2. ...but descend into directories so the allows below can match.
!*/

# 3. Explicitly allowed: project scaffolding and generic templates only.
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!LICENSE
!screenshot-fan.jpg
!screenshot-admin.jpg
!overview.mp4
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!Dockerfile
!.dockerignore
!docker-compose.yml
!docker/**
!.github/**
!templates/**
!.claude/**

# docs/ and tests/ stay local-only for now — this repo is being pushed as a
# small paused snapshot. They get tracked again once this is inherited into
# the scaled-up private repo.

# Machine-specific: absolute paths and per-session temp dirs. Shared settings
# live in .claude/settings.json, which is tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Application code. Generic — holds no creator data, so it is tracked.
!cookbook/**
!web/**
!runtime/**
!service/**

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. HARD BLOCK — filled-in creator data. Never tracked, no matter
#    what gets allowed above. This is the line that matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
/media/
*.mov
*.private.md
*.local.md
conversation.txt

# Runtime logs — request/response payloads, scraped profile data, real
# handles hit during dev testing. Not application code, so none of section
# 3's wholesale allows (service/** etc.) should ever have reached these —
# a bare "logs/" matches at any depth, so this blocks every one of them,
# current and future, instead of naming each wholesale-allowed dir by hand.
logs/

# Secrets and machine-specific generated config. Blocked even inside
# cookbook/, which section 3 allows wholesale.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/
**/stack.json

# Build noise that section 3's wholesale allow would otherwise pick up.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# graphify's own tool cache/index — local-only, matches at any depth like logs/.
graphify-out/

# impeccable skill's tool cache — local-only, matches at any depth.
.impeccable/

# Model weights. Tens of GB of binaries — never in git, whatever else changes.
models/

# Third-party binaries (llama.cpp release zips and their extracted contents).
vendor/

# Anything that looks like a filled-in instance, wherever it lands
character_bible.md
sources.md
character.md
!templates/character.template.md
!templates/sources.template.md

# .claude/worktrees/ holds live git worktrees — never track their contents,
# even though .claude/** is allowed above.
.claude/worktrees/


# /brag output — local-only render artifacts (the README video is allowed by name above).
brag-output*/
